Source: unroot
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Daniel Robbins <drobbins@breezyops.com>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 g++,
 libsubid-dev,
 make,
 python3,
 python3-pytest
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://kernel-seeds.org/projects/unroot/
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: unroot
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 tar,
 uidmap
@QEMU_RECOMMENDS@
Suggests: gzip, xz-utils, zstd
Description: daemonless Linux rootfs and cross-architecture toolkit
 Unroot enters, runs, creates, and transports Linux root filesystems using
 namespaces, durable subordinate-ID mappings, and optional QEMU user-mode
 emulation. It supports unprivileged rich roots, native host-owned roots,
 single-identity namespace execution, and faithful rootfs archives without a
 resident container daemon.
